@page "/pricing"
@attribute [MarketingPage]
@layout MarketingLayout

<SeoHeadContent Title="Hosting and pricing"
                Description="Choose this Relio instance or run your own. Learn about self-hosting requirements, optional mail delivery and the current availability of hosted billing."
                CanonicalPath="/pricing" />

<header>
    <p class="rl-marketing-eyebrow">Choose where Relio runs</p>
    <h1>Hosting choices</h1>
    <p class="rl-marketing-lead">Use an existing instance, or take responsibility for your own notebook's home.</p>
</header>

<section class="rl-marketing-section" aria-labelledby="instance-heading">
    <h2 id="instance-heading">Use this instance</h2>
    <p>You are viewing an instance of Relio. Its operator decides who can register and is responsible
        for hosting, mail delivery, backups and any published policies. Sign in if you already have an
        account, or create one when registration is available.</p>
    <MarketingStartLink ShowSignIn="true" />
    <p>No commercial offers are published here. Hosted billing and approved plan information are
        not implemented yet; enabling a provider setting alone does not make a paid service available.</p>
    <RelioPolicyLinks AriaLabel="Available policies for this instance" />
</section>

<section id="self-hosting" class="rl-marketing-section" aria-labelledby="self-hosting-heading">
    <h2 id="self-hosting-heading">Run your own instance</h2>
    <p>Relio's source is available under the AGPL. The same relationship features run without a
        billing provider or hosted product metrics. No paid entitlement is required by the current app.</p>
    <p>You will need .NET 10, SQL Server, HTTPS, and durable externally stored Data Protection keys
        protected by a certificate or the supported Windows protection mode.
        Keep the database, keys and required decryption material backed up together.</p>
    <p>Apply migrations before a production upgrade. Configure SMTP only if you want confirmation,
        password-reset and reminder emails. Without it, the dashboard still works, but
        email-based password recovery is unavailable.</p>
    <p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/docs/self-hosting.md">self-hosting deployment guide</a>,
        the <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/README.md#getting-started">setup instructions</a>
        and <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/docs/security/data-protection.md">protected-key guidance</a>
        before running an instance. <a href="https://github.com/kasuken/Relio/blob/main/LICENSE">Read the AGPL license</a>
        for your source-availability obligations.</p>
</section>

<section class="rl-marketing-section rl-marketing-faq" aria-labelledby="hosting-faq-heading">
    <h2 id="hosting-faq-heading">Hosting questions</h2>
    <details><summary>Can I use Relio without hosted services?</summary><p>Yes. The relationship workspace
        does not need billing or analytics. Optional hosted product metrics are off by default,
        and there are no browser tracking scripts.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Who can create an account?</summary><p>The operator chooses Open, InviteOnly or Closed
        registration. A fresh instance always allows its first account so it can get an administrator.
        Invitation-only instances need an invitation link after that first account.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is mail delivery required?</summary><p>No. With Email:Provider=None, the app sends no
        email. Configure SMTP to enable account confirmation, password-reset links and optional reminder
        emails, then review the instance's delivery and privacy responsibilities.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I move my notebook later?</summary><p>Export full JSON from Settings and restore it
        into a fresh account. Contact-only vCard export is also available. Neither export contains your
        password or authentication secrets. Backups and their retention remain the operator's responsibility.</p></details>
</section>
